course: dictionary
lesson: 4640
title: Hippo, the river giant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hippo is a huge, heavy African animal with a wide mouth, short legs and thick skin. You can use the clues around a word to build its meaning, and the words huge, heavy and thick skin tell you this is a big, strong animal.
explain: «Hippos spend the day in water and come out at night to eat grass.» The word spend shows they stay in the river for most of the day, and come out at night tells you they are not in the water all the time. Read the sentence again and check that your meaning fits.
explain: «Hippos cannot really swim or float; their heavy bones make them sink.» The word really is a clue: it tells you that hippos are not good swimmers, even though they live in water. So they walk along the bottom of the river and push up for air.
fact: A hippo is a huge, heavy African animal with a wide mouth, short legs and thick skin.
fact: Hippos spend most of the day in rivers and lakes, and come out at night to graze on grass.
fact: Hippos cannot really swim or float, so they walk along the riverbed and push up for air.
fact: The name hippo is short for hippopotamus, which means «river horse» in Greek.
fact: Hippos are among the most dangerous large animals in Africa because they are very territorial.
exercise: «Hippos spend the day in water and come out at night to eat grass.» When do hippos come out of the water to eat? | At lunchtime | *At night | Only in winter | In the morning
exercise: «Hippos cannot really swim or float; their heavy bones make them sink.» Why do hippos walk along the riverbed? | *Because their heavy bones make them sink | Because they are too lazy to swim | Because they like the mud | Because they are too small to swim
exercise: Hippo is short for a longer word. Which one is it? | *Hippopotamus | Crocodile | Elephant | Hippocampus
test: A hippo is a huge, heavy African animal. What does huge mean? | Very dark | Very small | *Very big | Very quiet
test: «Hippos are among the most dangerous large animals in Africa because they are very territorial.» What does territorial mean? | *Likes to guard its own area | Likes to sleep all day | Likes eating fish | Likes to travel far away
exam: Which statement about hippos is true? | Hippos eat only fish from the sea | *Hippos spend most of the day in rivers and lakes | Hippos are small animals with short tails and long wings | Hippos fly over rivers at night
